    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.weakly_connected_components - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.weakly_connected_components.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.weakly_connected_components()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get all weakly connected components as sets of node IDs.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.weakly_connected_components()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get all weakly connected components as sets of node IDs.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.weakly_connected_components()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n  .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get all weakly connected components as sets of node IDs.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet all weakly connected components as sets of node IDs.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L81434-L81506){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.weakly_connected_components()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Weakly connected components](../assets/graphs/weakly-connected-components.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A directed graph: a cycle A to B to C to A, a one-way edge C to D, a two-way pair D and E, and a separate edge F to G. Ignoring arrow direction leaves two pieces, A to E in the accent color and F, G in teal, which the card lists as the two weak components.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nFor undirected graphs, returns regular connected components. For directed graphs, treats all\nedges as undirected (ignoring direction) when finding components.\n\nA weakly connected component is a maximal set of nodes where every node is reachable from\nevery other node when edge directions are ignored.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[set[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   List of sets, where each set contains the node IDs in a component. Components are\n    returned in no particular order.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~node_connected_component`) \n\n:   The component of a single node.\n\n[](`~strongly_connected_components`) \n\n:   The components that follow edge directions.\n\n[](`~count_weakly_connected_components`) \n\n:   The number of components alone.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIgnoring edge direction, this graph has two separate pairs of nodes, so it returns two\nsets of node IDs:\n\n::: {#65166015 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"X\", \"Y\")], directed=True)\n\nlabel = graph.get_label_from_id\n[sorted(label(n) for n in c) for c in graph.weakly_connected_components()]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[['X', 'Y'], ['A', 'B']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nAn isolated node next to a chain of 10 is a second component, and `max()` picks out the\nlargest:\n\n::: {#59a97612 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nchain = ec.Graph().add_path_graph(10)\nchain.add_node(label=\"isolated\")\n\ncomponents = chain.weakly_connected_components()\nlen(components), len(max(components, key=len))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(2, 10)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Cut off by a closure\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network. Closing Riverside cuts the harbor off from\nthe rest of the city: the three harbor stations are left as a piece of their own:\n\n::: {#2fdd50a1 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\nmetro.delete_node(\"Riverside\")\n\nlabel = metro.get_label_from_id\npieces = sorted(metro.weakly_connected_components(), key=len)\n[sorted(label(n) for n in piece) for piece in pieces[:-1]]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n[['Docks', 'Harbor', 'Shipyard']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#f85b7b77 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npiece = {\n    n: f\"piece {i + 1}\" for i, nodes in enumerate(pieces) for n in nodes\n}\nmetro.set_node_attrs(\"piece\", piece)\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"piece\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#9